## Verify Configuration Before Boot

Before booting compute nodes, verify that boot-service and metadata-service are
configured correctly. These checks catch the most common failures before a
wasted boot cycle.

Confirm that boot-service has the boot configuration and its cloud-init source:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify the boot configuration is uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k boot config list -F yaml | grep ds=nocloud-net
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Confirm that the metadata-service has the cloud-init defaults:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify the cloud-init defaults are uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k metadata defaults list -F yaml | grep base_url
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Confirm that the metadata-service has the `compute` group:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify the cloud-init compute group is uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k metadata group list -F yaml | grep 'name: compute$'
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Finally, confirm that boot-service and metadata-service know each compute node.
Both services pick up new nodes from SMD on a timer, so wait until both know
every node before booting. The meta-data check goes to the metadata-service
container directly, because haproxy replaces the `X-Forwarded-For` header that
carries the node's address. `--noproxy '*'` keeps an `http_proxy` set in the
environment out of these requests; a proxy cannot reach the container.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Find the metadata-service's container address -->
```bash
metadata_ip=$(podman inspect metadata-service \
	| jq -r '.[].NetworkSettings.Networks[].IPAddress')
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

To check one node, the boot script should have a `kernel` line, and the
meta-data the node's own `instance-id`:

```bash
curl -fsS --noproxy '*' "http://${sms_ip}:8081/boot-service/bootscript?mac=${c_mac[0]}"
curl -fsS --noproxy '*' -H "X-Forwarded-For: ${c_ip[0]}" \
	"http://${metadata_ip}:8080/meta-data"
```

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Wait for the boot-service and metadata-service to resolve each compute node -->
<!-- ohpc_command for ((i=0; i<num_computes; i++)); do -->
<!-- ohpc_command     for ((t=0; ; t++)); do -->
<!-- ohpc_command         boot=0; meta=0 -->
<!-- ohpc_command         curl -fsS -m 5 --noproxy '*' "http://${sms_ip}:8081/boot-service/bootscript?mac=${c_mac[$i]}" \ -->
<!-- ohpc_command             | grep -q "^kernel " && boot=1 -->
<!-- ohpc_command         curl -fsS -m 5 --noproxy '*' -H "X-Forwarded-For: ${c_ip[$i]}" "http://${metadata_ip}:8080/meta-data" \ -->
<!-- ohpc_command             | grep -qx "instance-id: x1000c0s0b$((i+1))n0" && meta=1 -->
<!-- ohpc_command         (( boot && meta )) && break -->
<!-- ohpc_command         (( t < 132 )) || { echo "pre-boot node: FAILED for ${c_name[$i]} (boot-service=${boot} metadata-service=${meta})"; exit 1; } -->
<!-- ohpc_command         echo "Waiting for ${c_name[$i]}: boot-service=${boot} metadata-service=${meta}" -->
<!-- ohpc_command         sleep 5 -->
<!-- ohpc_command     done -->
<!-- ohpc_command done -->
<!-- ohpc_command echo "pre-boot node: OK" -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
